# What goes in the sdist beyond the `clops` package itself.
#
# The sdist ships the test suite, and two tests lint/show `examples.my_company`
# — so the example library has to come along or `pytest` on an unpacked sdist
# fails. `examples` is deliberately NOT an installed package (see
# pyproject.toml); grafting it here puts it in the sdist only, never the wheel.

# setuptools' legacy sdist default only auto-globs `test*.py`, which silently
# dropped `tests/conftest.py` and `tests/__init__.py` — so the sdist shipped a
# test suite that could not pass (40 failures from an uncleared registry).
# Graft the directory so what ships is what runs.
graft tests

graft examples

# Docs are listed one by one, NOT grafted. Not everything in `docs/` is written
# for users, and an sdist on PyPI is public and permanent — a `graft docs` would
# ship whatever happens to be sitting there the day you cut a release. These six
# are the ones the README links.
include docs/philosophy.md
include docs/concepts.md
include docs/patterns.md
include docs/examples.md
include docs/combinators.md
include authoring-spec.md

include server.json

# Never ship build/scratch artifacts.
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude .DS_Store
prune **/__pycache__
prune .claude
prune .github
prune landing-page
prune smoke-tests
# Deployment examples are for people reading the repo, not for people who
# `pip install clops-mcp`.
prune deploy
# Never-public working notes. `internal/` is gitignored, but an sdist is built
# from the working directory rather than from git — so .gitignore alone would
# not stop it shipping. Belt and braces, on the one directory where the cost of
# being wrong is permanent.
prune internal
